WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.230
Hello CZsWorld,

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:09.050
I know this isn't the type of content you
would usually expect from me, but I'm feeling

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.640
kind of experimental right now, so let me
know if this is something you'd like to see

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:17.160
from me in this poll right here, and don't
worry, this doesn't count as my video for

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:20.390
this week, just something I thought I'd try
out.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:24.609
So here we see the Death Note falling into
the human world as it should, the one difference

00:00:24.609 --> 00:00:28.480
being that it falls into an area where Light
is sitting by himself, as opposed to in the

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.730
anime where he just notices it fall past the
window and happens to be the first one to

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:33.730
pick it up.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:34.920
So what's the difference?

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:39.330
In this film, you could say that the Shinigami
who dropped it is giving it to Light on purpose,

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:42.250
knowing full-well what he is capable of doing
with it.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:46.210
You'll notice that the Death Note itself has
some strange new markings on the top corners.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:50.170
This could be something as simple as the book
having been removed from the chain that Ryuk

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:51.930
uses to sling it around his shoulder.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:55.550
That would mean that in this movie, Light
actually has Ryuk's Death Note, whereas in

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:58.960
the anime, he has the Death Note that Ryuk
stole from Sidoh.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.600
So Ryuk may not have multiple notebooks in
this version.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:02.950
Here he is.

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:03.950
Here's Ryuk.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:04.950
Looks great in this light.

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.260
No pun intended.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:11.220
Gods of Death love apples, and here we see
an apple moving on it's own, but also other

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:12.750
objects in this room swirling around.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:16.820
I can't say for sure if the presence of a
Shinigami is what is causing that swirling,

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:21.079
but I will say that if it is, it could be
even more of a security threat to Light.

00:01:21.079 --> 00:01:25.060
In the anime he had to worry about Ryuk simply
picking up and eating apple on camera, as

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:29.049
it would appear like a floating apple that
disappears to the naked eye, but this swirling

00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:32.080
phenomenon could prove to be much more of
a distraction.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:37.049
OK, so the film takes place in Seattle because
this is an American version of Death Note,

00:01:37.049 --> 00:01:40.360
but why Seattle as opposed to any other American
city?

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.159
My theory is that it's the most reminiscent
of Tokyo.

00:01:43.159 --> 00:01:45.890
Both cities feature a tall skinny observation
tower.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.619
In Seattle it's the Space Needle.

00:01:47.619 --> 00:01:49.720
In Tokyo, it's Tokyo Tower.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:52.170
Both have a Ferris Wheel on their skyline
as well.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.390
As you'll see later, the Ferris Wheel comes
into play in the plot somehow.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:02:00.389
I couldn't find any real high schools abbreviated
with the letters NSH in Seattle, but let me

00:02:00.389 --> 00:02:02.569
know if you can find any in the comments.

00:02:02.569 --> 00:02:06.170
What's interesting here is that this girl
on the right looks more like Misa Amane, mostly

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:10.860
just because of her hair, but this girl in
the middle looks to be an actress named Margaret

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:11.860
Qualley.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:15.000
According to IMDb, she's playing a character
named Mia Sutton.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.260
Misa, Mia S...

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.610
It seems like Mia may be the American counterpart.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:23.190
It would also seem that she is a little bit
younger if she's still in high school and

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:27.490
she probably isn't a celebrity any more, maybe
just a popular cheerleader instead.

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:28.740
Also she smokes now.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:33.170
Unless that's Matt, and they've turned him
female for this movie...

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:34.170
Just kidding.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:38.010
It's hard to tell from this lighting, but
it looks like this guy might be Lakeith Stanfield,

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:42.510
the actor who's playing L. If so, this is
a big departure from the usual white-shirt

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.319
and blue jeans L we are used to.

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:47.870
He's also wearing this mask that covers half
of his face, which could be paired with a

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:50.970
visor or glasses of some sort to protect his
identity.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:55.580
As you probably know, Kira needs a name and
a face to kill someone using the Death Note.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:59.580
On Light's desk, we see another apple and
some kind of little propeller based machine,

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.209
maybe a drone of some kind.

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:05.110
This tells us not only that Light is still
a genius in this adaptation, but also could

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:09.010
foreshadow the use of a helicopter later,
which if you've seen the show, you know that

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:12.459
one of the most pivotal turning points in
the series takes place while Light is in a

00:03:12.459 --> 00:03:13.769
helicopter.

00:03:13.769 --> 00:03:17.970
In this shot we learn that Light is left-handed,
as opposed to him being right-handed in the

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:20.120
series and the Japanese adaptations.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:24.049
That makes me wonder if this will be used
against him in this movie.

00:03:24.049 --> 00:03:27.720
If you aren't aware, left-handed writers tend
to run their hand against the page when writing

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:31.829
in English or any other language that goes
from left to right and as a result their hand

00:03:31.829 --> 00:03:34.530
smudges against the text that they have just
written.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:38.689
L could use this to determine that Kira is
left handed if he were to obtain the notebook.

00:03:38.689 --> 00:03:42.810
This also narrows down the search a lot, considering
most people are right-handed.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:46.989
This area has the same red lighting as the
area where we saw L walking before, meaning

00:03:46.989 --> 00:03:50.370
that L may actually be investigating the scene
of the crime himself.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:54.520
This, once again goes against what we are
accustomed to with L's character.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:58.750
In the light novel The Los Angeles BB Murder
Cases, we learn that L likes to work behind

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.959
the scenes and sends Naomi Misora to do the
physical investigation for him.

00:04:02.959 --> 00:04:06.939
We also see the name Kira being used, which
is noteworthy considering the characters have

00:04:06.939 --> 00:04:11.380
been given Americanized names, like Light
Turner instead of Light Yagami and Mia Sutton

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:12.970
instead of Misa Amane.

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:16.930
But in the anime, the name Kira originates
from the Japanese pronunciation of the English

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:21.250
word "Killer", so perhaps Japan does play
some part in this movie after all.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:25.850
In the anime, Kira does occasionally leave
little calling cards or false clues to L when

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:29.190
he kills criminals, but for the most part
just leaves the media to come up with the

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:31.240
idea of Kira on their own.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.540
This message on the wall seems much more blatant.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:37.160
Here's this girl again, and if this is her
making out with Light, then there is a good

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:40.030
chance that she is in fact supposed to be
Misa.

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:44.020
Unless of course, director Adam Wingard is
just throwing us a curveball and that is actually

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:47.820
Kiyomi Takada, which would make some sense
because of the fact that Light meets her in

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:51.650
college in the anime so he could just be meeting
her in high school in this film.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:54.960
Towards the end of the trailer we see this
Ferris Wheel getting crushed and Light seems

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:56.160
to be saving someone.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.680
This leads me to ponder a few possibilities.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:02.310
Is this a part of one of Light's plans, much
like how he causes the catastrophe on the

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.550
bus to learn more about Raye Penber?

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:07.180
Is this the work of a Shinigami trying to
get their Death Note back?

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:11.340
I only suggest this because of the way the
Ferris Wheels bends in, as if an invisible

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.040
force is crushing it.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.760
And one more possibility is that someone else
has a Death Note and they are trying to kill

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:19.840
someone on the Ferris Wheel or send a message
to Light.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:22.670
Let me know what you think in the comments
below.

